{
 "v": 2,
 "doc": "The expert catalogue (docs/proposed/MOE-v1.md). One small model per item of the iron-tier chain. `makes` = the item it produces (a key of `goal.have`); `needs` = what the expert must already hold (its prerequisites; the router calls other experts until they are met); `goal` = what ends an episode in success (items held, `#log`/`#planks` = any species, or a progress entry reached); `start` = the standardised start distribution the expert is trained on (kit ranges drawn at the start of every episode, junk the expert must ignore, ores placed around the start); `max_steps` = commands per episode. Wood comes in several species, so a kit lists them as separate ranges. Every craft belongs to the expert of its result (planks, stick, crafting_table, ...), so no expert calls a crafting expert (owner 2026-11-08); `equivalent` lists items that satisfy a need of another item (a stone pickaxe is a wooden pickaxe for mining); movement and escape experts are not in v1. v2 (docs/proposed/MOE-v2.md): `targets` = the scan groups (log, coal, iron, way, sky) the router shows the expert; `kind: skill` = a movement expert (`move`: walk to the nearest relevant target; `unstick`: dig or climb out to the surface) that the router calls at any time and that makes no item (`goal.reach` = blocks from the target at success); `variants` = further scenario files of one expert.",
